VALUES ('27e90bdb-1547-48d2-9ae5-4cfda2cd5e02', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 40, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for umbilical hernia repair in a pediatric patient, as distinguished from an adult patient?');
VALUES ('27e90bdb-1547-48d2-9ae5-4cfda2cd5e02', '7fc2225f-2193-4ffb-a000-6b3aab101cb5', 'This reinforces the age-based and complexity-based (incarcerated vs. reducible) code-distinction themes already established elsewhere (tonsillectomy, fracture care) applied to umbilical hernia repair specifically — genuine, documented clinical factors that can determine correct code selection.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering neurosurgery/spine and hernia repair; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('5772a53d-f53b-459c-b55a-3966af21d0bb', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 41, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for an incarcerated or strangulated hernia repair, as distinguished from a routine, reducible hernia repair?');
VALUES ('5772a53d-f53b-459c-b55a-3966af21d0bb', '3ec19ed4-fc30-467f-af05-7b848191be77', 'This reinforces the complexity-reflects-code-selection theme applied specifically to hernia presentation severity — incarcerated/strangulated status is a genuine, commonly distinct code-selection factor, not merely a scheduling-urgency consideration with no coding relevance.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering neurosurgery/spine and hernia repair; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('e421e703-5b1f-4930-b2e7-6041ad049ac9', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 42, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when bowel resection is required due to strangulated, non-viable bowel found during an incarcerated hernia repair?');
VALUES ('e421e703-5b1f-4930-b2e7-6041ad049ac9', '7c9083aa-14f9-45f6-b5c2-3d32695b8033', 'This reapplies the general genuinely-distinct-additional-component separate-reportability principle (already established for excision-plus-repair, debridement-plus-VAC, and other multi-component scenarios) to incarcerated hernia repair complicated by bowel resection.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering neurosurgery/spine and hernia repair; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('9db60d2f-2fda-469d-b61b-e953304b553b', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 43, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a diagnostic lumbar puncture (spinal tap) performed for cerebrospinal fluid analysis, as distinguished from a therapeutic lumbar puncture performed to relieve elevated intracranial pressure?');
VALUES ('9db60d2f-2fda-469d-b61b-e953304b553b', 'f894cf03-9151-4fe7-b542-b321905b3231', 'This reapplies the diagnostic-versus-therapeutic distinction (already established for thoracentesis/paracentesis Drainage coding) to lumbar puncture — a recurring CPT coding pattern across multiple different anatomic/procedural contexts.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering neurosurgery/spine and hernia repair; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('55a0983e-8a74-4f09-a5fa-d023ed4f73e3', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 44, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for placement of a ventriculoperitoneal (VP) shunt for hydrocephalus?');
VALUES ('55a0983e-8a74-4f09-a5fa-d023ed4f73e3', 'ea46e80a-e68d-4672-a8f6-88a1818ed5bc', 'VP shunt placement (a specific, defined neurosurgical CSF-diversion procedure) has its own specific code — distinct from both a diagnostic/therapeutic lumbar puncture and from external ventricular drain placement (a different, typically temporary CSF-diversion technique with its own distinct code).', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering neurosurgery/spine and hernia repair; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('cac23bed-45bc-4c97-88d1-7092f1ff4d43', '161a5441-b93a-4090-955b-3ea097d0b2fe', 45, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for VP shunt revision (addressing shunt malfunction) versus initial VP shunt placement?');
